'''Prem Singh Yadav''' is an Indian scientist whose research focuses on [[Cloning|buffalo cloning]]<ref name="src-d03b0f5819">{{cite web|url=https://www.moneycontrol.com/news/india/cibr-scientists-clone-7-elite-m-29-buffaloes-re-clone-one-5561561.html|title=CIBR scientists clone 7 elite M-29 buffaloes, re-clone one|website=Moneycontrol|date=17 July 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220929222324/https://www.moneycontrol.com/news/india/cibr-scientists-clone-7-elite-m-29-buffaloes-re-clone-one-5561561.html|archive-date=29 September 2022}}</ref>.
Yadav headed the buffalo-cloning team at [[Central Institute for Research on Buffaloes|ICAR-CIRB]] in [[Hissar|Hisar]]<ref name="src-d03b0f5819" />.
In 2017, Yadav's team produced Sach-Gaurav, described by NDTV as India's first cloned Assamese buffalo<ref name="src-b4ab04664d">{{cite web|url=https://www.ndtv.com/india-news/indias-first-cloned-assamese-buffalo-born-1824454|title=India’s First Cloned Assamese Buffalo Born|website=NDTV|date=15 March 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190811220112/https://www.ndtv.com/india-news/indias-first-cloned-assamese-buffalo-born-1824454|archive-date=11 August 2019}}</ref>.
Yadav led the Animal and Fisheries Sciences team that received the 2019 Nanaji Deshmukh [[Indian Council of Agricultural Research|ICAR]] Award for Outstanding Interdisciplinary Team Research; ICAR recorded 12 eligible applications for the two 2019 categories<ref name="src-4deaa5ee4f">{{cite web|url=https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/2022-08/ICAR_Citations_final_2020_Low_0.pdf|title=ICAR Award 2019 Citations|website=Indian Council of Agricultural Research|date=2020}}</ref>.

==Career==
Yadav joined the Indian Council of Agricultural Research as a scientist on 12 April 1993<ref name="src-e73557644a">{{cite web|url=https://cirb.res.in/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/Staff-Remuneration-List-Hisar-2023.pdf|title=Scientists Remunerations|website=ICAR-Central Institute for Research on Buffaloes|date=2023}}</ref>. In 2003, while a senior scientist, Yadav began a 12-month Department of Biotechnology overseas associateship in [[Neustadt, Hesse|Neustadt]], Germany<ref name="src-75cd616383">{{cite web|url=https://icar.org.in/sites/default/files/inline-files/PARTNERSHIP-AND-LINKAGES-02_0.pdf|title=ICAR Partnership and Linkages: Overseas training during 2003–04|website=Indian Council of Agricultural Research|date=2003}}</ref>. Yadav undertook a research stay at the Institute for Farm Animal Genetics in Germany from 28 December 2010 to 10 February 2011<ref name="src-4fdcf94f36">{{cite web|url=https://cirb.res.in/wp-content/uploads/2018/01/annualreport2010-2011.pdf|title=ICAR-Central Institute for Research on Buffaloes Annual Report 2010–11|website=ICAR-Central Institute for Research on Buffaloes|date=2010–11}}</ref>. He later served as head of [[Central Institute for Research on Buffaloes|ICAR-CIRB]]'s Division of Animal Physiology and Reproduction<ref name="src-87ac8ccc96">{{cite web|url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210723192859/https://cirb.icar.gov.in/ps-yadav/|title=Dr. Prem Singh Yadav|website=ICAR-Central Institute for Research on Buffaloes (archived official profile)|date=23 July 2021}}</ref>. Yadav retired from [[Central Institute for Research on Buffaloes|ICAR-CIRB]] as a principal scientist in 2025<ref name="src-30cdb84a23">{{cite web|url=https://www.amarujala.com/haryana/rewari/principal-scientist-dr-prem-singh-retired-rewari-news-c-198-1-rew1001-218880-2025-05-03|title=प्रधान वैज्ञानिक डॉ. प्रेम सिंह हुए सेवानिवृत्त|website=Amar Ujala|date=3 May 2025}}</ref>.

==Research==
In 2015, a team led by Yadav produced Hisar Gaurav, a cloned [[Murrah buffalo|Murrah]] bull; ICAR described [[Central Institute for Research on Buffaloes|CIRB]] as India's second centre to produce a cloned buffalo<ref name="src-443a3f8b23">{{cite web|url=https://icar.gov.in/node/4887|title=ICAR-CIRB become India’s second center to produce cloned buffalo|website=icar.gov.in|date=2016}}</ref>. Yadav led the ICAR-CIRB project that used semen from Hisar Gaurav to produce 20 calves through artificial insemination by 2018<ref name="src-12f91675f5">{{cite web|url=https://www.tribuneindia.com/news/archive/haryana/cloned-bull-s-semen-used-to-produce-20-calves-in-8-months-698521/|title=Cloned bull's semen used to produce 20 calves in 8 months|website=The Tribune|date=14 December 2018}}</ref>. In 2020, a team led by Yadav produced seven clones of the elite breeding bull M-29 and a re-clone of Hisar Gaurav<ref name="src-edb32eef83">{{cite web|url=https://www.amarujala.com/haryana/hisar/cirb-hisar-has-created-seven-cloned-pieces-one-re-clone-hisar-news-rtk5643533104|title=सीआईआरबी हिसार ने तैयार किए सात क्लोन कटड़े, एक री-क्लोन भी बनाया|website=Amar Ujala|date=17 July 2020}}</ref>. By 2022, [[Central Institute for Research on Buffaloes|CIRB]] had produced about 14,000 semen doses from Hisar Gaurav and distributed them free to farmers in villages of Nuh district<ref name="src-a26d426313">{{cite web|url=https://www.etvbharat.com/english/bharat/hisar-gaurav-first-cloned-calf-born-at-icar-cirb-turns-7/na20221211201520284284768|title='Hisar Gaurav', first cloned calf born at ICAR-CIRB, turns 7|website=ETV Bharat|date=11 December 2022}}</ref>. Research led by Yadav found that female progeny of Hisar Gaurav produced 300–600 litres more milk per lactation<ref name="src-e4007d0265">{{cite web|url=https://www.kisantak.in/animal-husbandry/story/indias-first-clone-pt-bull-hisar-gaurav-in-cirb-increase-milking-and-re-production-nsr-1135812-2024-12-11|title=PT Bull: भैंसों का विक्की डोनर है ये बुल, रिसर्च में इस्तेमाल होता है सीमेन, पढ़ें इसकी खूबियां|website=Kisan Tak|date=11 December 2024}}</ref>.

==Selected publications==
* Yadav was first author of a 2024 Theriogenology study evaluating growth, health, telomere length and semen characteristics in cloned and re-cloned buffalo bulls<ref name="src-f264a3ee95">{{cite web|url=https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/37793222/|title=Evaluation of postnatal growth, hematology, telomere length and semen attributes of multiple clones and re-clone of superior buffalo breeding bulls|website=PubMed|date=2024}}</ref>.
* Yadav co-authored a 2020 [[PLOS One|PLOS ONE]] study of the semen characteristics and fertility of a cloned water buffalo bull<ref name="src-a15f669816">{{cite web|url=https://journals.plos.org/plosone/article?id=10.1371/journal.pone.0237766|title=Semen parameters and fertility potency of a cloned water buffalo bull produced from a semen-derived epithelial cell|website=PLOS ONE|date=21 August 2020}}</ref>.
* Yadav co-designed the research and was a corresponding author of the 2019 [[Scientific Reports]] paper “Successful cloning of a superior buffalo bull”<ref name="src-9c0f3d0c0c">{{cite web|url=https://www.nature.com/articles/s41598-019-47909-8|title=Successful cloning of a superior buffalo bull|website=Scientific Reports|date=6 August 2019}}</ref>.
* Yadav co-authored a 2019 peer-reviewed review chapter on telomerase structure, regulation and measurement<ref name="src-8d2b29b28d">{{cite web|url=https://doi.org/10.5772/intechopen.89506|title=Telomerase Structure and Function, Activity and Its Regulation with Emerging Methods of Measurement in Eukaryotes|website=doi.org|date=24 December 2019}}</ref>.
* Yadav co-authored the book “Reproductive Biotechnology in Buffalo” (ISBN 8189304801)<ref name="src-11b51d3d09">{{cite web|url=https://ndri.res.in/sites/default/files/2025-06/ASAP%20April-2025.pdf|title=List of Indian e-Books of ASAP Publication (2018-20)|website=ICAR-National Dairy Research Institute|date=April 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251028060629/https://ndri.res.in/sites/default/files/2025-06/ASAP%20April-2025.pdf|archive-date=28 October 2025}}</ref>.
* Yadav was first author of the 2005 paper “Bovine ICM derived cells express the Oct4 ortholog” in Molecular Reproduction and Development<ref name="src-0c979bd135">{{cite web|url=https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/15973686/|title=Bovine ICM derived cells express the Oct4 ortholog|website=PubMed|date=2005}}</ref>.

